    {
      "id": "p0239-b003",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "Sans suddenly stops acting like a goofball, turns deadly serious, and begins to speak in an intimidating tone of voice. To preserve this attitude change in the Japanese script, the translator replaced his normal Japanese speech patterns with harsher speech patterns. For example, instead of his usual, laid-back personal pronoun oira, Sans now uses the more assertive pronoun ore. And instead of referring to the main character with the casual second-person pronoun an ta, he now uses the more condescending pronoun omae.",
        "raw": "Sans suddenly stops acting like a goofball, turns deadly serious, and begins to\nspeak in an intimidating tone of voice. To preserve this attitude change in the\nJapanese script, the translator replaced his normal Japanese speech patterns\nwith harsher speech patterns. For example, instead of his usual, laid-back\npersonal pronoun oira, Sans now uses the more assertive pronoun ore. And\ninstead of referring to the main character with the casual second-person\npronoun an ta, he now uses the more condescending pronoun omae.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.09625583,
          0.23977143,
          0.68795089,
          0.36235
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.09422426,
          0.23905714,
          0.70025206,
          0.36342143
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          13,
          14,
          15,
          16,
          17,
          18,
          19
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "Sans 突然收起嬉皮笑脸，变得严肃而可怕，话语里满是威慑。为了保留这种态度转变，译者把他平时的日语说话方式改得更强硬。例如，原本随意的自称 oira（我）换成了更强势的 ore（我）；称呼主角时，也从较随便的 anta（你）变成了更居高临下的 omae（你）。",
        "status": "draft",
