    {
      "id": "p0239-b008",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "Because both of these surprise meanings rely on English abbreviations and English spelling, this wordplay would likely be lost in a straightforward, literal translation. To compensate for this, the localization team kept the English words mostly as-is, then included their Japanese meanings afterward for clarification. This solution preserves Toby's original intent without forcing Japanese words to awkwardly fit the English abbreviations.",
        "raw": "Because both of these surprise meanings rely on English abbreviations and\nEnglish spelling, this wordplay would likely be lost in a straightforward, literal\ntranslation. To compensate for this, the localization team kept the English\nwords mostly as-is, then included their Japanese meanings afterward for\nclarification. This solution preserves Toby's original intent without forcing\nJapanese words to awkwardly fit the English abbreviations.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.09625583,
          0.78991429,
          0.69822049,
          0.89464286
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.09422426,
          0.7892,
          0.70025206,
          0.89571429
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          47,
          48,
          49,
          50,
          51,
          52
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "这两处反转都依赖英语缩写和拼写，直接照字面翻译，很可能丢掉文字游戏。为此，团队基本保留了英文词语，再附上日语解释。这样既保留了 Toby 的意图，也不用勉强拼出能对应英语缩写的日语词。",
        "status": "draft",
        "spans": []
      },
